# Checks rather than writes, so a commit is never quietly different from what was staged.
# `pnpm format` is the one that fixes formatting.
#
# The whole repo is checked, not just the staged files: a partial stage can pass in isolation and
# still break the build, which is the failure this exists to catch. The full run is about five
# seconds, so narrowing it would buy nothing.
pnpm lint && pnpm knip && pnpm test
